Lifting State Up

	Right now expenses is a plain constant in App. - it can never actually change.

	"Lifting State  Up" means: when two or more components need to share or affect same data, move that data's state to their closest common parent - here APP itself.

	App already sits above both NewExpense (which produces new expenses) and Expenses (which displays them) - the natural home for shared state.



Stateful vs Statless components:
	- A components that manages its own state (expenses, now) is called a stateful component.
		A component that just receives and displays props (ExpenseItem, ExpenseFilter) is stateless component


.map - transforms EVERY item in an array into a NEW array - here, an array of JSX elements, one per expense, of ANY length


Why this erorr - key in the list should be available?
-------
	- 	When array changes, React compares the NEW list of elements to the OLD list.
		Without any way to tell items apart individually, React can only compare them POSITIONALLY (item 1 vs item 1, item2 vs item2..)

	- React then just overwrites each position's content to match - which is wasteful, and DANGEROUS the moment ExpenseItem holds its OWN internal state per instance - that per-instance state can end up attached to the WRONG logical expense.
	

	- Give react explicit, STABLE identity for each item via the key prop, so React can match old items to new items by IDENTITY, not position.



