What?
	React - JavaScript Library for building user interfaces.


Why not just JavaScript?
	- Manually using document.getElementByID(...).innerHTML ==> across 100+ elements quickly becomes combersome, error-prone, and hard to maintain
	- React offers simpler mental model: 
		Describe - WHAT UI Should look like for given state,
		let React figure out the actual DOM instructions


	Imperative (Vanilla JS) - you give step-by-step instructiions: 'find this element, then change its text, then add this class..'
	Declarative (React)		- you describe the DESIRED END STATE , react works out the DOM changes needed to get there.



